This license defines the terms of use of the source code
of the "Screenwriter" application (the "Project"), hosted
on GitHub in the repository of the developer DarkEye.

1. PERMITTED

1.1. To view, study and use the source code of the Project
     for personal, educational and non-commercial purposes.

1.2. To create forks of the repository for improvements,
     bug fixes and pull requests to the author.

1.3. To use individual fragments of the code (no more than
     20% of the total volume) in your own non-commercial
     projects, provided that the copyright notice is preserved.

1.4. To reference the Project in articles, reviews and
     educational materials with attribution.

2. PROHIBITED

2.1. To use the Project or its substantial parts (more than
     20% of the code) to create commercial applications,
     products or services without the written permission
     of the author.

2.2. To publish derivative versions of the Project in app
     stores (Google Play, RuStore, App Store, etc.) under
     your own name.

2.3. To remove or modify copyright notices, the name
     "Screenwriter" and mentions of the developer DarkEye.

2.4. To sell, sublicense or transfer the Project to third
     parties for commercial purposes.

2.5. To use the name "Screenwriter" and the logo of the
     Project in your own products without permission.

3. DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTIES

The Project is provided "as is", without any warranties,
express or implied, including warranties of merchantability,
fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement.

The author is not liable for any damages arising from the
use or inability to use the Project.

4. FEEDBACK

All suggestions, fixes and pull requests are welcome and may
